                            <comment id="17928345" author="JIRAUSER298470" created="Wed, 19 Feb 2025 08:38:14 +0000"  >&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;RootCause%26DevDesign&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Root Cause &amp;amp; Dev Design&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Unify the Truncate logic and remove redundant implementations. &#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Known limitations of this solution: &#160;&lt;br/&gt;
The usage form of truncate(Column, Column) is restricted by Spark&apos;s BinaryExpression logic. The dataType cannot dynamically adjust each return type based on the actual value of the second parameter&apos;s column. Therefore, the type of the first parameter will still be used. However, this usage form is expected to be uncommon.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
